Look closely:

> [DAY1 11:53:09 - DAY1 11:53:22]  
>I turn my head to the right. I bent forward. Katrina: Seems like, I'm swaying back and forth, and I'm talking. Katrina: We don't need to provide lunch, but we can offer some sweets. Yes, yes, afternoon tea. I nodded and turned my head to the left. Yes, right, so no need to provide lunch. I nodded my head to the right. I'm still speaking. Everyone can come over after lunch. I'm looking at the whiteboard. Then we can adjust the timeline.

Key phrase: "**afternoon tea**"

Now consider common meanings—"Afternoon Tea"—typically refers to traditional British-style light meal served midday including sandwiches, scones, pastries & drinks usually enjoyed during early-to-mid-afternoon hours (~4 PM). Often includes sweet treats ("some sweets") along with finger foods.

This strongly points away from American burger joints like McDonald's/KFC/Dico/Wallace—which aren't typically labeled serving full-scale Afternoon Teas.

In fact, while certain places serve snacks/desserts later day—they rarely call service itself "afternoon tea."

Only exception might involve upscale cafes offering formal versions—for example Starbucks has limited offerings under same label occasionally—but generally considered luxury item rather than standard office snack break solution.

Moreover, note wording used:"offer some sweets", followed immediately afterward saying "...everyone comes over _after_ lunch".

That means main event = Lunch first→then gathering happens afterwards involving desserts/sweets.

And crucially—we hear ZERO discussion about WHERE people should get meals—from outside vendors vs internal provision.

Instead focus remains entirely on logistics concerning timing (“adjust timelines”) versus destination selection.

Given complete silence across entire passage about choosing locations—including neither verbalized preference nor suggestion—to select amongst AB CD list seems unjustified because non-existent basis within source material.

Conclusion therefore: No valid reason supports picking any individual alternative out of five possibilities presented above.

