INFO:__main__:ID 34 Answer: The conversation discusses food options for dining during the event. The group decides against providing lunch since "we don’t need to provide lunch" according to Katrinas statement. Instead, sweet snacks such as cake were considered suitable alternatives ("afternoon tea"). However, later discussion shifts toward having something substantial around dinnertime—specifically mentioning “ordering pizza” which implies eating pizza instead of other meal types listed. Since none among these mentions include any specific dish except Pizza being discussed explicitly under possible dinners; however option isn't present hence considering only available ones:

KFC – No mention  
Hot pot – Mentioned neither  

